t "]},"amounted to €88 million, compared to €103 million in 2025. This contraction can be explained on one hand by a start to the year strongly marked by the negative effects of surplus milk supply in a market saturated by a drop in demand. On the other hand, the integration of chocolate activities contributed negatively over the period, impacted by the Middle East crisis, and a negative effect of inventory valuation in the context of declining quotations."]},{"type":"p","children":["At €13 million, Other operating costs and income decreased by €6 million. ",{"type":"b","children":["Net Income Group share "]},"was €38 million, almost stable compared to 2025."]},{"type":"p","children":["SAVENCIA ",{"type":"b","children":["Net financial debt"]}," stood at €815 million, compared to €464 million in 2025, an increase of €351 million in connection with the two strategic acquisitions made during the half-year."]},{"type":"p","children":["*****"]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["The Group's CSR commitment"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["This first half of 2026 marks the launch of the Group’s renewed CSR commitments and whose ambitions have been projected for ten years."]},{"type":"p","children":["In regard to environment, the decarbonization trajectory is aligned by design with that validated by the SBTi (Science Based Target initiative): 1.5° by 2035 and net zero by 2050."]},{"type":"p","children":["Efforts are continuing in all areas. In terms of scope 1 and 2, energy-saving measures have been deployed on all sites, integrating managerial routines, and energy conversion projects are gradually being extended."]},{"type":"p","children":["The challenge of reducing water consumption also remains an operational priority through numerous projects on all sites."]},{"type":"p","children":["*****"]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Like-for-like figures (considering an integration effect on January 1, 2026, of SAVENCIA Gourmet's Chocolate activities"